!!! Text Editor

Use the template `$:/plugins/rimir/theme/rr-text-editor` for an `<$edit-text>`-based body editor that picks up the standard EditorToolbar keyboard shortcuts (bold, italic, headings, autolist if the `sq/editor-autolist` plugin is installed) and binds Ctrl+Enter to clear an edit-state tiddler.

Caller passes parameters via `<$let>`:

|!Variable |!Required |!Purpose |
|`editTiddler` |Yes |Title of the tiddler whose `text` field is being edited |
|`editState` |Yes |State tiddler that gates edit mode (cleared on Ctrl+Enter) |
|`wrapClass` |Yes |CSS class for the outer wrapper div (controls width, height, etc.) |
|`editAutoFocus` |No |`"yes"` to auto-focus the textarea on mount (default `"no"`) |
|`editFocusSelectFromStart` |No |Selection-start offset on auto-focus (default `99999` → past end → no selection) |
|`editFocusSelectFromEnd` |No |Selection-end offset on auto-focus (default `0` → caret at end) |

```
<$let editTiddler=<<myNote>> editState="$:/state/my-edit" wrapClass="my-editor">
<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/theme/rr-text-editor"/>
</$let>
```

Internally renders toolbar children inside `<$edit-text>` so TW's framed editor engine binds shortcuts; the toolbar itself is hidden via `.rr-text-editor-host > .tc-editor-toolbar { display: none }`. Style the visible iframe via `<<wrapClass>> iframe.tc-edit-texteditor`.

!!! Double-click-to-edit

Companion template `$:/plugins/rimir/theme/rr-text-view-editable` wraps a block-mode transclude in an `<$eventcatcher>` that sets a caller-supplied `editState` tiddler to `"yes"` on double-click — pairs with `rr-text-editor` so the same `editState` flips both directions (dblclick → enter, Ctrl+Enter → leave). Before flipping the state it fires `<$action-clear-selection>` so the dblclick word-selection is wiped — otherwise the new textarea would mount with the matching range still highlighted blue.

|!Variable |!Purpose |
|`editState` |State tiddler set to `"yes"` on dblclick |
|`viewTiddler` |(Optional) tiddler to transclude. If unset, uses surrounding `<$tiddler>`/currentTiddler context |

```
<$let editState=<<myEditState>> viewTiddler=<<myNote>>>
<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/theme/rr-text-view-editable" $mode="block"/>
</$let>
```

Adds class `rr-text-view-editable` (with `cursor: text`) to the wrapper div.

!!! `<$action-clear-selection>`

Action widget that calls `window.getSelection().removeAllRanges()`. Drop it into any action sequence that needs to wipe a stray browser text-selection (e.g. before swapping a rendered view for an editor). Used internally by `rr-text-view-editable`; usable directly anywhere actions run.

```
<$button>
<$action-clear-selection/>
<$action-setfield $tiddler="$:/state/edit" text="yes"/>
Edit
</$button>
```

